Gears of War 3: green speckle and off colours over the whole image at 2x internal resolution, part 1.
The game builds its colour grading lookup table each frame (pixel shader 5FD384E4DE20CAC8) from a
256x16 strip of 16 side-by-side slices, sampled bilinearly at coordinates derived from the pass's
interpolants. At 1x every fetch lands on a strip texel centre. With resolution scaling the host pixels
sit off the guest pixel centres: fetches at a slice edge blend in the neighbouring slice and the slice
index can wrap, so table entries get wrong colours. Found with debug_point_ps.txt (0056).
gpu_guest_pixel_center_ps (default 5FD384E4DE20CAC8, restart): for the listed pixel shaders, with
resolution scaling, the interpolants are moved to the centre of the guest pixel (v + ddx(v) * dx +
ddy(v) * dy), so every host pixel computes the 1x entry. 0059 then makes the table a 1x texture (a
scaled copy of duplicated entries bands when filtered). No change at 1x or for other shaders.

