+// Gears of War 3 recomp. Gears 3 builds its colour grading lookup table each
+// frame (pixel shader 5FD384E4DE20CAC8) from a 256x16 strip of 16 side-by-side
+// slices, sampled bilinearly at coordinates derived from the pass's
+// interpolants. At 1x every fetch lands on a strip texel centre. With
+// resolution scaling the host pixels sit off the guest pixel centres: fetches at
+// a slice edge blend in the neighbouring slice (another blue level) and the
+// slice index can wrap, so table entries get wrong colours (green speckle over
+// the whole image at 2x). Evaluated at the guest pixel centre, every host pixel
+// computes the 1x entry; gpu_unscaled_resolve_max_pitch then makes the table a
+// 1x texture (a scaled copy of duplicated entries bands when filtered).
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_STRING(gpu_guest_pixel_center_ps, "5FD384E4DE20CAC8", "GPU",
+                      "With resolution scaling, pixel shaders (comma-separated ucode hashes) whose "
+                      "interpolants are evaluated at the centre of the guest pixel, as at 1x, instead "
+                      "of each host pixel. For passes that compute table indices from their "
+                      "coordinates (Gears of War 3's colour grading table)")
+    .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kRequiresRestart);
+
